strong|8-K filed 2026-11-04, items 2.02,5.07,9.01|APP gapped up in after-hours trading after AppLovin’s Q3 results beat expectations and its Q4 outlook came in ahead of consensus.

Revenue rose 55% year over year to about $2.185 billion, and diluted EPS was $4.30 versus the $4.03 analysts expected. Net income climbed 72% to about $1.44 billion. Management said a partial rollout of upgraded AI advertising models improved advertiser results and encouraged higher spending; it also said the rollout still has room to expand. The company added $3.2 billion to its buyback authorization, bringing the total to $3.6 billion.

